<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<widgets>

	<!--
		A direct transcription of MOD V2's own <widget-groupings> block,
		which is lines 373-439 of the DONOR's shortcuts/overrides.xml, not of
		anything in this skin. Estuary 8 has no overrides.xml: v3 never reads one,
		so it was removed. Read the donor copy, which is pinned in-tree at
		reference/modv2-Piers-551f77b0/shortcuts/overrides.xml and matches the
		commit recorded in UPSTREAM.lock. Nothing here is invented.

		The whole design turns on ONE home window property. script-skinshortcuts.xml
		sets it before opening the type picker and clears it before opening a slot
		picker:

		  10005 "Set type of widgets"  -> SetProperty(WidgetVisibility,True,home)
		  1475..1483 "Select widget N" -> ClearProperty(WidgetVisibility,home)

		So one picker shows two completely different trees. With the property SET
		you choose the item's widget TYPE and get exactly three rows: None,
		Preconfigured widgets, Widgets to personalize. With it CLEAR you are
		filling one of the nine personal slots and get the video/music/pictures/
		add-ons content tree instead.

		What you choose then dictates the rest of the pane: the eight "Select
		widget N" rows are gated on Property(widget)=PersonalWidgetList and the
		single panel row on PersonalWidgetPanel, and each slot's appearance and
		sort rows only appear once widgetPath.N has a value.

		The 15 type entries carry no <path>. They are names MOD V2's Home.xml
		routes on, and the panel behind each is hand-written markup there, which
		is why type="custom".

		v2 content name -> v3 (source, target), from the nine sources v3 accepts:
		  video          -> nodes/video          videosources   -> sources/video
		  music          -> nodes/music          musicsources   -> sources/music
		  playlist-video -> playlists/video      picturesources -> sources/pictures
		  playlist-audio -> playlists/music      addon-image    -> addons/image
		  addon-video    -> addons/video         addon-audio    -> addons/audio
		  addon-program-plugin -> addons/executable
	-->

	<!-- ============ widget TYPE picker: WidgetVisibility is set ============ -->

	<group name="preconfigured" label="$LOCALIZE[31327]"
	       visible="!String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<widget name="DiscWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[427]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/disc.png" visible="System.HasMediaDVD"/>
		<widget name="MoviesWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[342]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/movies.png"/>
		<widget name="TVShowsWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[20343]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/tv.png"/>
		<widget name="MusicWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[2]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/music.png"/>
		<widget name="MusicVideosWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[20389]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/musicvideos.png"/>
		<widget name="LiveTVWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[19020]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/livetv.png"/>
		<widget name="RadioWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[19021]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/radio.png"/>
		<widget name="GamesWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[15016]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/games.png" visible="System.GetBool(gamesgeneral.enable)"/>
		<widget name="AddonsWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[24001]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/addons.png"/>
		<widget name="PicturesWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[1]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/pictures.png"/>
		<widget name="VideoWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[3]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/videos.png"/>
		<widget name="FavoritesWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[10134]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/favourites.png"/>
		<widget name="WeatherWidget" label="$LOCALIZE[8]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/sidemenu/weather.png"/>
	</group>

	<group name="personalize" label="$LOCALIZE[31404]"
	       visible="!String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<widget name="PersonalWidgetList" label="$LOCALIZE[31366]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/PersonalList.png"/>
		<widget name="PersonalWidgetPanel" label="$LOCALIZE[31405]" type="custom" target="videos"
		        icon="icons/PersonalPanel.png"/>
	</group>

	<!-- ====== slot picker: WidgetVisibility is clear ======
		(the donor's four such nodes are at reference/modv2-Piers-551f77b0/
		shortcuts/overrides.xml:393, :405, :417 and :420)

		The nesting is MOD V2's: a top-level <content> that yields Kodi's own
		library nodes, plus hand-declared sub-groups. That means Kodi's node
		labels and these group labels land in the SAME list, so they must not
		read the same words. Under Music they did: the node list carries
		"Sources" and the group carried $ADDON[32075], also "Sources", word for
		word. The ids MOD V2 used are Skin Shortcuts' own and v3 renumbered them,
		so 32040 "Playlist" now sat next to Kodi's "Playlists" too.

		Retargeted to the media-specific v3 strings, which no Kodi node uses:
		  videos-playlists 32040 -> 32004 "Video Playlist"
		  videos-sources   32075 -> 32069 "Video Source"
		  music-playlists  32040 -> 32005 "Music Playlist"
		  music-sources    32075 -> 32073 "Music Source"

		The two add-on groups keep 32010 / 32011 ("Video Add-On", "Music
		Add-On"): they already read differently from Kodi's "Video add-ons" /
		"Music add-ons" nodes, and the two are genuinely different destinations,
		measured on the bench: the node commits library://video/addons.xml/ and
		the group commits addons://sources/video/.
	-->

	<group name="videos" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32030]"
	       visible="String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<content source="nodes" target="video"/>
		<group name="videos-playlists" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32004]">
			<content source="playlists" target="video"/>
		</group>
		<group name="videos-addons" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32010]">
			<content source="addons" target="video"/>
		</group>
		<group name="videos-sources" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32069]">
			<content source="sources" target="video"/>
		</group>
	</group>

	<group name="music" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32031]"
	       visible="String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<content source="nodes" target="music"/>
		<group name="music-playlists" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32005]">
			<content source="playlists" target="music"/>
		</group>
		<group name="music-addons" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32011]">
			<content source="addons" target="audio"/>
		</group>
		<group name="music-sources" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32073]">
			<content source="sources" target="music"/>
		</group>
	</group>

	<group name="pictures" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32020]"
	       visible="String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<content source="sources" target="pictures"/>
	</group>

	<group name="addons" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32007]"
	       visible="String.IsEmpty(Window(home).Property(WidgetVisibility))">
		<group name="addons-programs" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32009]">
			<content source="addons" target="executable"/>
		</group>
		<group name="addons-video" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32010]">
			<content source="addons" target="video"/>
		</group>
		<group name="addons-music" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32011]">
			<content source="addons" target="audio"/>
		</group>
		<!-- target is "pictures", NOT "image", and the difference is visible to the
		     user. Both are ACCEPTED for source="addons" and add-on resolution IS
		     identical either way, because _ADDONS_TARGET_ALIASES
		     (providers/content.py:47-59) carries "image" at :52 and "pictures" at
		     :55 and folds both onto the same JSON-RPC "image" content.

		     Every line number in this comment is against the script.estuary8.shortcuts
		     3.0.1 SOURCE, which is the only authority available: the add-on ships
		     no docs/ directory and no markdown at all. Verify against
		     ~/Library/Application Support/Kodi/addons/script.estuary8.shortcuts/,
		     read-only, and never edit it.

		     The divergence is downstream: TARGET_MAP
		     (constants.py:81-90) carries "images" and "pictures" but NOT "image",
		     so _map_target_to_window (dialog/pickers.py:462-466) falls through to
		     "videos", addon_type is computed as "video" (pickers.py:555-561), and
		     picking a PICTURE add-on offers Movies / TV Shows / Episodes.
		     With "pictures", pickers.py:477-478 returns the type directly and the
		     "Select Widget Type" dialog never opens at all. -->
		<group name="addons-pictures" label="$ADDON[script.estuary8.shortcuts 32012]">
			<content source="addons" target="pictures"/>
		</group>
		<!-- MOD V2 listed the four <content> nodes above AND four
		     addons://sources/<type> shortcuts, and this file transcribed both.
		     In v3 they land in ONE flat list, and they are DUPLICATES: measured
		     on the bench, "Video Add-On >" (the content node) and
		     "Video add-ons >" (the shortcut) both open the identical two rows,
		     "Create menu item to here" and "POV >". Same for Program, Music and
		     Picture. Eight rows, four destinations, near-identical wording: a
		     user who backs out of one and takes its twin has gone in a circle,
		     which is exactly what the widget picker was reported to do.

		     The four duplicates are removed. The content nodes are kept because
		     they carry the curated $ADDON labels and resolve per-add-on icons.
		     androidapp://sources/apps has no twin, so it stays. -->
		<!-- type is "programs", plural. The singular "program" is not a widget
		     type: the set is in constants.py WIDGET_TYPES and the singular is not
		     in it. Nothing validates the value, so the wrong one is accepted in
		     silence, lands in widgetType, and matches no template anywhere. This
		     is the same defect as target="image" in this file, found and fixed
		     the day before; the sweep that found this one covered every target=
		     and type= in all five shortcut files, on 2026-07-31.

		     It is also load-bearing beyond the property: _browse_widget_path
		     takes any non-empty declared type in preference to prompting, so
		     both spellings suppress the "Select Widget Type" dialog. Only the
		     stored value differed, which is why this never showed a symptom and
		     would have started producing one the moment a template read it. -->
		<widget name="addon-browse-android" label="$LOCALIZE[20244]" type="programs"
		        target="programs" source="addon" browse="true" icon="DefaultAddonProgram.png"
		        visible="System.Platform.Android">
			<path>androidapp://sources/apps</path>
		</widget>
	</group>

</widgets>
